.TH NN-GRAPH 1 "2026" "nn 0.1.0" "NN Manual"
.SH NAME
nn-graph \- export the compute graph
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nn graph [options] <model>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Write the graph as text, DOT, mermaid, or JSON. No GUI.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-format FMT
dot, mermaid, json, or text.
.TP
.B \-\-from NODE
Start node.
.TP
.B \-\-to NODE
End node.
.TP
.B \-\-op TYPE
Filter op type.
.TP
.B \-\-depth N
Neighborhood depth.
.TP
.B \-\-collapse\-activations
Collapse activations.
.TP
.B \-\-collapse\-constants
Collapse constants.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
nn graph model.onnx --format dot
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
nn-inspect(1), nn-ops(1)
